---
<BaseLayout title={`${sys.name}: CRM software for small business`} description={description} imageAlt="BIZOMAT CRM: customers, leads and deals in one shared place" breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Systems', href: SYSTEMS_HOME }, { label: sys.name, href: sys.url }]}
  schema={[
    { '@type': 'SoftwareApplication', name: sys.name, alternateName: ['BIZOMAT Customer Relationship Management', sys.kind], url: `${SITE.url}${sys.url}`, applicationCategory: 'BusinessApplication', operatingSystem: 'Web browser', description, publisher: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#organization` } },
    { '@type': 'FAQPage', url: `${SITE.url}${sys.url}#faq`, mainEntity: questions.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })) },
  ]}>
  <section class="pp-hero" aria-labelledby="crm-title">
    <Container class="pp-hero__inner">
      <div>
        <p class="bz-eyebrow">{sys.name} · {sys.kind}<span class="pp-hero__formerly">Formerly {sys.formerly}</span></p>
        <h1 id="crm-title">{CRM.headline}</h1>
        <p class="pp-hero__lead">{sys.name} is a Customer Relationship Management (CRM) system for small businesses and their teams: one shared place for your contacts, companies, leads, deals and follow-ups. Work your pipeline on a board, plan every activity and see what is closing from live reports.</p>
        <div class="pp-hero__actions">
          <Button href={access.href} variant="accent" rel="noopener" data-cta="crm-access">{access.label}</Button>
          <Button href={GUIDE} variant="secondary" data-cta="crm-guide">Read the user guide</Button>
        </div>
        <p class="pp-hero__note">{access.note} Sign-in required: use your BIZOMAT account, the same one as {finance.name} and {projects.name}. New to BIZOMAT? Create an account on the sign-in page.</p>
      </div>
      <CrmPipeline id="crm-hero" />
    </Container>
  </section>

  <section class="pp-section" id="what" aria-labelledby="what-title">
    <Container>
      <div class="pp-head">
        <p class="bz-eyebrow">What it does</p>
        <h2 id="what-title">Every customer, and every conversation with them, in one place</h2>
        <p>Customer relationship management is how a business keeps track of the people it sells to and everything said and agreed with them. {sys.name} keeps contacts, companies, leads, deals and activities on shared records, so anyone on the team can pick up where a colleague left off.</p>
        <StatusLegend />
      </div>
      <ul class="pp-cards" role="list">
        {CRM.capabilities.map((c) => <li class="pp-card"><span class="pp-card__mark"></span><h3>{c.title} <StatusLabel status="live" /></h3><p>{c.text}</p></li>)}
      </ul>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <section class="pp-section pp-section--tint" id="who" aria-labelledby="who-title">
    <Container>
      <div class="pp-head">
        <p class="bz-eyebrow">Who it is for</p>
        <h2 id="who-title">Who should use it</h2>
        <p>Any business that sells to other people and wants one shared record of its customers. Someone working alone can use it too: register in your own name.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="pp-cards" role="list">
        {audiences.map((a) => <li class="pp-card"><h3>{a.t}</h3><p>{a.x}</p></li>)}
      </ul>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <section class="pp-section" id="problems" aria-labelledby="problems-title">
    <Container>
      <div class="pp-head">
        <p class="bz-eyebrow">Problems it solves</p>
        <h2 id="problems-title">What changes when the team shares one CRM</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="pp-cards pp-cards--2" role="list">
        {problems.map((p) => <li class="pp-card"><h3>{p.t} <StatusLabel status={p.s} /></h3><p>{p.x}</p></li>)}
      </ul>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <section class="pp-section pp-section--tint" id="features" aria-labelledby="features-title">
    <Container>
      <div class="pp-head">
        <p class="bz-eyebrow">Features</p>
        <h2 id="features-title">Every feature, explained</h2>
        <p>What {sys.name} does today, area by area, and what is planned. The <a href={GUIDE}>user guide</a> shows where each working feature is in the application.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pp-tools">
        <section id="records" aria-labelledby="records-title">
          <h3 id="records-title">Leads, contacts and companies <StatusLabel status="live" /></h3>
          <dl>{records.map((r) => <div><dt>{r.t}</dt><dd>{r.x}</dd></div>)}</dl>
        </section>
        <section id="pipeline" aria-labelledby="pipeline-title">
          <h3 id="pipeline-title">Pipelines and deals <StatusLabel status="live" /></h3>
          <dl>
            <div><dt>Stages</dt><dd>A new organisation starts with a sales pipeline of {CRM.stages.length} stages: {list(CRM.stages.map((s) => `${s.name} (${s.probability}%)`))}. Rename them, add your own, set each stage's probability, or add more pipelines.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>The board</dt><dd>Drag a deal to the next stage, or onto Won or Lost; a menu on each card does the same from the keyboard.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Each deal</dt><dd>Keeps its value, products and services, contacts, competitors and the time it spent in each stage.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Weighted value</dt><dd>Value times probability. It feeds the forecast.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Won or Lost</dt><dd>Closed deals leave the board and count in the reports. A lost deal records why.</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </section>
        <section id="activities" aria-labelledby="activities-title">
          <h3 id="activities-title">Activities and follow-ups <StatusLabel status="live" /></h3>
          <dl>
            <div><dt>Plan every follow-up</dt><dd>Plan every call, meeting and visit against the customer and the deal, and assign it with a due date and a priority.</dd></div>
            {activities.map((a) => <div><dt>{a.t}</dt><dd>{a.x}</dd></div>)}
            <div><dt>Log emails</dt><dd>Write to a contact from a template. Your own mail program sends it, and the CRM logs it on the record (<a href="#integrations">more below</a>).</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </section>
        <section id="reports" aria-labelledby="reports-title">
          <h3 id="reports-title">Dashboard and reports <StatusLabel status="live" /></h3>
          <dl>
            <div><dt>Overview</dt><dd>Open pipeline, weighted forecast, value won, win rate, new leads, lead conversion, contacts and companies, and overdue follow-ups, with charts below. Computed from your records when you open it (<a href="#dashboard">figure by figure</a>).</dd></div>
            <div><dt>{CRM.reports.length} reports</dt><dd>{list(CRM.reports.map((r, i) => (i ? r.toLowerCase() : r)))}.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Each report</dt><dd>Its figures, a chart, a table and CSV export. Filter by dates, owner, team and pipeline.</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </section>
        <section id="automations" aria-labelledby="auto-title">
          <h3 id="auto-title">Automations <StatusLabel status="live" /></h3>
          <dl>
            <div><dt>How they work</dt><dd>An automation is a trigger, conditions and actions. Each event runs an automation once, and every run is kept in its history.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Triggers</dt><dd>A new or reassigned lead, a lead changing status, a new contact, a deal being created, entering a stage, won, lost or close to its expected close date, and an activity being assigned or becoming overdue.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Actions</dt><dd>Notify people, create a follow-up, set a priority, flag a deal or assign an owner.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Ready-made</dt><dd>Every new organisation starts with these {CRM.automations.length}: {list(CRM.automations.map((a, i) => (i ? a.charAt(0).toLowerCase() + a.slice(1) : a)))}. Switch any of them off, change them, or add your own.</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </section>
        <section id="roles" aria-labelledby="roles-title">
          <h3 id="roles-title">Organisations, teams and roles <StatusLabel status="live" /></h3>
          <dl>
            <div><dt>Organisations</dt><dd>Create one for each business you run, belong to several, and switch between them. Invite colleagues and group them into teams.</dd></div>
            {CRM.roles.map((r) => <div><dt>{r.name}</dt><dd>{r.text}</dd></div>)}
            <div><dt>Permissions</dt><dd>Owners and administrators can fine-tune what the other roles may view, create, edit, delete, import and export.</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </section>
        <section id="data" aria-labelledby="data-title">
          <h3 id="data-title">Search, views and your data <StatusLabel status="live" /></h3>
          <dl>{data.map((d) => <div><dt>{d.t}</dt><dd>{d.x}</dd></div>)}</dl>
        </section>
        <section id="security" aria-labelledby="sec-title">
          <h3 id="sec-title">Accounts and security <StatusLabel status="live" /></h3>
          <ul class="pp-list">{security.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}</ul>
        </section>
        <section id="planned" aria-labelledby="planned-title">
          <h3 id="planned-title">Not built yet</h3>
          <dl>{planned.map((w) => <div><dt>{w.t} <StatusLabel status="planned" /></dt><dd>{w.x}</dd></div>)}</dl>
        </section>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  {(shots.length > 0 || erpShot) && (
    <section class="pp-section" id="screens" aria-labelledby="screens-title">
      <Container>
        <div class="pp-head">
          <p class="bz-eyebrow">Screenshots</p>
          <h2 id="screens-title">The real product</h2>
          <p>Captured from the running application with a fictional organisation and example data. More screens are in the <a href={GUIDE}>user guide</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pp-shots">
          {erpShot && (
            <figure class="pp-shot">
              <img src={erpShot.src} alt={`${erpShot.title}. ${erpShot.caption}`} width="1440" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <figcaption><span>Inside {erp.name}. {erpShot.caption} Choose {sys.module} in the module rail to open it.</span><span class="viz__tag viz__tag--real">Product screen</span></figcaption>
            </figure>
          )}
          {shots.map((s) => (
            <figure class="pp-shot">
              <img src={s.src} alt={`${s.title}. ${s.caption}`} width="1440" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <figcaption><span>{s.title.replace(/^[^:]+: /, '').replace(/^a /, 'A ')}. {s.caption}</span><span class="viz__tag viz__tag--real">Product screen</span></figcaption>
            </figure>
          ))}
        </div>
      </Container>
    </section>
  )}

  <section class="pp-section pp-section--tint" id="dashboard" aria-labelledby="dashboard-title">
    <Container>
      <div class="pp-head">
        <p class="bz-eyebrow">The main dashboard</p>
        <h2 id="dashboard-title">The Overview, figure by figure</h2>
        <p>The Overview is the CRM's dashboard. Every figure is computed from your records when you open it, and each one opens the list or report behind it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pp-tools">
        <section aria-labelledby="d-figures">
          <h3 id="d-figures">The figures <StatusLabel status="live" /></h3>
          <dl>{figures.map((f) => <div><dt>{f.t}</dt><dd>{f.x}</dd></div>)}</dl>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="d-charts">
          <h3 id="d-charts">Charts and lists <StatusLabel status="live" /></h3>
          <dl>{charts.map((f) => <div><dt>{f.t}</dt><dd>{f.x}</dd></div>)}</dl>
        </section>
      </div>
      <p class="pp-table-note">Choose a period or exact dates and a person (Everyone, Me or a colleague); where you have them, a team and a pipeline. Every role sees the Overview by default; owners and administrators can change that in Settings, Permissions.</p>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <section class="pp-section" id="walkthrough" aria-labelledby="walkthrough-title">
    <Container>
      <div class="pp-head">
        <p class="bz-eyebrow">Screen by screen</p>
        <h2 id="walkthrough-title">What each screen is for</h2>
        <p><StatusLabel status="live" /> The CRM's menu lists these screens, and every one works today. Your role decides which ones you see.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="pp-cards" role="list">
        {screens.map((s) => <li class="pp-card"><h3>{s.t}</h3><p><strong>You see:</strong> {s.see}</p><p><strong>You do:</strong> {s.do}</p></li>)}
      </ul>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <section class="pp-section pp-section--tint" id="start" aria-labelledby="start-title">
    <Container class="pp-split">
      <div>
        <p class="bz-eyebrow">Getting started</p>
        <h2 id="start-title">Start in {steps.length} steps</h2>
        <p class="pp-head-lead">The <a href={GUIDE}>user guide</a> walks through each step, and everything after it, screen by screen.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="pp-steps">
        {steps.map((s) => <li><h3>{s.t}</h3><p>{s.x}</p></li>)}
      </ol>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <section class="pp-section" id="workflows" aria-labelledby="workflows-title">
    <Container>
      <div class="pp-head">
        <p class="bz-eyebrow">Typical workflows</p>
        <h2 id="workflows-title">How the work flows through the CRM</h2>
        <p>Four common jobs, step by step. The steps that reach {finance.name} and {projects.name} need a company that runs them.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="pp-cards pp-cards--2" role="list">
        {workflows.map((w) => (
          <li class="pp-card">
            <h3>{w.t} <StatusLabel status={w.s} /></h3>
            <ol class="flow-steps">{w.steps.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}</ol>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <section class="pp-section pp-section--tint" id="integrations" aria-labelledby="int-title">
    <Container>
      <div class="pp-head">
        <p class="bz-eyebrow">Integration</p>
        <h2 id="int-title">How it works with the other BIZOMAT systems</h2>
        <p>Every link between BIZOMAT systems checks both tools' own permissions, joins records of tools that belong to the same company, and never copies money: figures are read from Finance when asked. Email, your calendar and CSV files connect too.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pp-tools">
        {integrations.map((g, i) => (
          <section aria-labelledby={`int-${i}`}>
            <h3 id={`int-${i}`}>{g.href ? <a href={g.href}>{g.t}</a> : g.t} {g.s && <StatusLabel status={g.s} />}</h3>
            <dl>{g.items.map((it) => <div><dt>{it.t} {!g.s && it.s && <StatusLabel status={it.s} />}</dt><dd>{it.x}</dd></div>)}</dl>
          </section>
        ))}
        <section aria-labelledby="int-works">
          <h3 id="int-works">Email, calendar and CSV <StatusLabel status="live" /></h3>
          <dl>{works.map((w) => <div><dt>{w.t}</dt><dd>{w.x}</dd></div>)}</dl>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="int-not">
          <h3 id="int-not">Gmail and Microsoft 365 <StatusLabel status="planned" /></h3>
          <p class="int-note">{planned[0].x}</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <section class="pp-section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <Container>
      <div class="pp-head">
        <p class="bz-eyebrow">Questions</p>
        <h2 id="faq-title">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      </div>
      <dl class="guide-faq">
        {questions.map((f) => <div><dt>{f.q}</dt><dd>{f.a}</dd></div>)}
      </dl>
      <p class="pp-table-note">Something not covered here? Read the <a href={GUIDE}>user guide</a> or <a href="/contact/">contact BIZOMAT</a>.</p>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <section class="pp-section pp-section--inverse" id="access" aria-labelledby="crm-cta">
    <Container class="pp-band">
      <h2 id="crm-cta">Open {sys.name} in {erp.name}.</h2>
      <div class="pp-band__actions">
        <Button href={access.href} variant="accent" rel="noopener" data-cta="crm-band-access">{access.label}</Button>
        <Button href={GUIDE} variant="secondary" data-cta="crm-band-guide">Read the user guide</Button>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <section class="pp-section" id="related" aria-labelledby="related-title">
    <Container>
      <div class="pp-head">
        <p class="bz-eyebrow">Related systems</p>
        <h2 id="related-title">The other BIZOMAT systems</h2>
        <p>One BIZOMAT account opens {sys.short}, {finance.short} and {projects.short} inside {erp.name}. <a href={SYSTEMS_HOME}>See all systems</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="pp-cards" role="list">
        {related.map((s) => (
          <li class="pp-card">
            <p class="related-kind">{s.status === 'available' ? s.kind : `${s.kind} · ${STATUS_LABEL[s.status]}`}</p>
            <h3><a href={s.url}>{s.name}</a></h3>
            <p>{s.line}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </Container>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .pp-head-lead { margin: .9rem 0 0; font-size: var(--step-1); line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .pp-tools > section[id] { scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--header-h) + 1rem); }
  .int-note { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: .92rem; }
  .flow-steps { display: grid; gap: .4rem; margin: .8rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.25rem; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: .96rem; }
  .pp-card .related-kind { margin: 0 0 .5rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: .8rem; }
  .guide-faq { display: grid; gap: 1rem; margin: 0; max-width: 52rem; }
  .guide-faq > div { padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); }
  .guide-faq dt { font-weight: 650; color: var(--ink); }
  .guide-faq dd { margin: .4rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-2); }
</style>
